      "side": 1,
      "message": "(Below is what you already know, documenting this on this CL in case someone comes looking for it in the future)\n\nget_current_interrupt_vector had some issues, and I patched some bugs with it in later patch set. It now returns an integer in 0-255, or 256 upon error. The error condition can occur when ISR\u003d0, see b:128444630. This means we won\u0027t be able to make use of get_current_interrupt_vector for now, and this macro-based solution may be the best option at the moment. Hopefully we figure out b:128444630 and get a little more elegant solution.",
